From 86cdd19e36b25f2f549839dd01a64a3596188556 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:04:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 286: the tape is its own exam - judgment moves from
 code into weights

285's smoke made the flaw undeniable: every judgment was hand-written,
the weights only copied whichever judge was pointed at them, and with two
judges the disagreement was one-sided - votes was simply always wrong
where they differed - so arbitration collapsed into trusting the better
heuristic.

This stage inverts the direction of teaching. Nobody demonstrates. The
signal is L = -log P(value(s) | evidence of the address with s hidden):
hide one mention, show the rest, require the hidden value. The label is
the tape, so there are as many examples as slots rather than a quota of
questions, and what the weights must learn is the thing the judges were
hand-written approximations of - weighing evidence. Votes and external
corroboration are demoted to features on the candidates; if arbitration
exists it emerges inside P and is measured, not coded.

UNKNOWN is a candidate whose target is real whenever the hidden value is
absent from the visible evidence, so honesty is trained rather than
assumed, and the answer is the argmax - no threshold constants, in 284's
sense. The separation invariant holds by construction: the mind predicts
a value of the tape given evidence from the tape, the tape resamples
during training, and scoring runs on a tape from a disjoint corpus.

Three relative examiners, none tunable. Beat BOTH hand-written judges at
leave-one-out on the held-out tape. Say UNKNOWN more when the answer is
absent than when present. And the lying tape: forge one visible mention
wholesale and keep beating votes - the forged value has no external
corroboration, so a mind that weighs evidence discounts it while votes by
construction cannot. Verified on a hand tape: hiding the only mention of
a value yields target UNKNOWN, and the injected lie turns votes into a
1-1 abstain while the corroboration feature still separates 1 to 0.

